<title>USA: Clinton, lawmakers avoided specifics on tax relief.</title>
<headline>Clinton, lawmakers avoided specifics on tax relief.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-11-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>President Bill Clinton and congressional leaders did not discuss tax relief in specific terms during a budget meeting Tuesday, the White House said.</p>
<p>&quot;They did not discuss specific areas of tax relief,&quot; White House spokesman Mike McCurry told reporters after Clinton and the Republican and Democratic leaders met.</p>
<p>McCurry said the meeting focused on how to balance the budget, which Clinton says is his top second term priority.</p>
</text>
